{"id":"mentoring-practice","title":"During practice","minutes":4,"summary":"Observe facts, support briefly and hand back.","mediaIds":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Your outcome","html":"<p>Observe facts, support briefly and hand back.</p><p>Estimated reading time; check at your own pace. This is developmental support, separate from qualifications and formal assessment.</p>"},{"heading":"Observe first","html":"<p>Unless a demonstration was agreed, let the coach lead. Capture two factual examples: what the adult did and what the children did next, without identifying children. “The explanation lasted through two restarts” is more useful than “poor communicator”. Keep observation windows short enough to maintain your assigned duties.</p>"},{"heading":"Make one useful adjustment","html":"<p>Offer a brief question or demonstration, or adjust space, numbers or challenge. Return ownership. Avoid long queues and explanations. Never use exclusion, exercise or humiliation as punishment for mistakes. Act immediately on safety concerns through the applicable procedure; do not wait for a debrief.</p>"},{"heading":"Illustrative volunteer example: support and passing","html":"<p>Start with a manageable 4v1, add a second defender when appropriate, then revisit support in a wider game. The 4v1 progression comes from the supplied mentoring proposal; it is not a newly verified Hub resource. The existing 4v2 Rondo is tagged U12/U14, so adapt cautiously rather than prescribe it to beginners. Ask about another passing option instead of calling every pass. Observe whether teammates offer choices and the coach allows decision time.</p>"},{"heading":"Existing resources and boundaries","html":"<p>Use Hide &amp; Seek for protecting and finding support, or a small 3v3 game adapted to the children. Hide &amp; Seek and 4v2 Rondo are verified Hub activities; the particular progressive sequence is an illustrative application. Practice constraints and bonus scoring do not alter official match rules. Review old conditions before reuse; do not revive punitive removal rules.</p>"}],"quiz":[{"id":"mentoring-practice-1","prompt":"Players are waiting in a long queue. What might help?","options":["A longer explanation to the whole group.","Consider smaller parallel games and observe involvement.","Punish the waiting players with exercise."],"correct":1,"explanation":"Change the organisation and check the effect rather than blame the children."},{"id":"mentoring-practice-2","prompt":"The mentor disagrees with a minor coaching choice. What should they do?","options":["Shout an alternative to the players.","Take control without asking.","Use the agreed quiet prompt or wait for private feedback."],"correct":2,"explanation":"Support ownership and avoid competing instructions."},{"id":"mentoring-practice-3","prompt":"An unsafe setup becomes apparent. What next?","options":["Act immediately through the safety procedure.","Wait until the debrief to protect ownership.","Treat it only as a quiz topic."],"correct":0,"explanation":"Immediate safety takes priority over the normal observation agreement."}],"takeaway":"Record two factual examples, one short intervention and the hand-back.","sourceRefs":[]}
